     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With h1_1:access and h1_2:escalate blocked, every path to crown:obtain is cut. The attacker can still reach edge0:reach, edge1:reach, h1_0:access, h2_0:obtain, h2_2:obtain and h4_0:access. h2_1:escalate (AND) needs the blocked h1_2:escalate, so it fails. That also stops h3_1:access (AND, needs h2_1). h3_0:obtain needs only the blocked h1_1:access, and h3_2:access needs only the blocked h1_2:escalate, so both fail. As a result h4_1:access (needs h2_1 or h3_2) and h4_2:access (needs h3_2) fail. At the top layer, h5_0:pivot needs h4_1, h5_1:traverse needs h3_0, h3_1 or h3_2, and h5_2:pivot (AND) needs h3_2, so all three fail. crown:obtain therefore has no reachable parent.\"}"
    }
